{"name":"Lunar Eclipse","hex":"#415053","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lunar eclipse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A phenomenon occurring when the Earth casts a shadow over the Moon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lunar_eclipse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lunar eclipse","blocks":[{"text":"A lunar eclipse, also called a blood moon, is an astronomical event that occurs when the Moon orbits through Earth's shadow.‍‍ Lunar eclipses occur during eclipse season, when the Moon's orbital plane is approximately in line with Earth and the Sun. The type and length of a lunar eclipse depend on the Moon's proximity to the lunar node.‍‍"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Lunar_eclipse_04-15-2014_by_R_Jay_GaBany.jpg/330px-Lunar_eclipse_04-15-2014_by_R_Jay_GaBany.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_eclipse","wikidata":"Q44235"},{"title":"Lunar Eclipse (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lunar Eclipse is a 1999 Chinese film and the directorial debut from Sixth Generation director Wang Quan'an. It is also the feature film debut of Wang's most frequent collaborator/muse Yu Nan. Unlike his next two films, which focus on rural communities, Lunar Eclipse is an urban drama following the wife of a newlywed couple who becomes mesmerized by an amateur photographer who claims to have once been in love with a woman who looked just like her. The film was produced by the Beijing Film Studio."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f0/Lunar_Eclipse_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lunar_Eclipse_(film)","wikidata":"Q6703659"},{"title":"Eclipse","blocks":[{"text":"An eclipse is an astronomical event which occurs when an astronomical object or spacecraft is temporarily obscured, by passing into the shadow of another body or by having another body pass between it and the viewer. This alignment of three celestial objects is known as a syzygy. An eclipse is the result of either an occultation or a transit. A \"deep eclipse\" is when a small astronomical object is behind a bigger one."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg/330px-Solar_eclipse_1999_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eclipse","wikidata":"Q141022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Eclipse_lunar_2019.gif/250px-Eclipse_lunar_2019.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a0/Eclipse_lunar_2019.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Eclipse_lunar_2019.gif/250px-Eclipse_lunar_2019.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Partiality of the eclipse on 17 July 2019 observed from Gloucestershire, UK","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEclipse_lunar_2019.gif"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/2007-03-03_-_Lunar_Eclipse_small-43img.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b6/2007-03-03_-_Lunar_Eclipse_small-43img.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Timelapse of the total lunar eclipse on 4 March 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2007-03-03_-_Lunar_Eclipse_small-43img.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Lunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png/500px-Lunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Lunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png/1280px-Lunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Lunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png/500px-Lunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"October 2014 lunar eclipse viewed from Minneapolis during sunrise on 8 October 2014. Both the Moon and Sun were visible at that time.‍[20]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALunar_eclipse_at_sunrise_Minneapolis_October_2014.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Full_Eclipse_of_the_Moon_as_seen_in_from_Irvine%2C_CA%2C_USA_%2852075715442%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Full_Eclipse_of_the_Moon_as_seen_in_from_Irvine%2C_CA%2C_USA_%2852075715442%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Full_Eclipse_of_the_Moon_as_seen_in_from_Irvine%2C_CA%2C_USA_%2852075715442%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Full_Eclipse_of_the_Moon_as_seen_in_from_Irvine%2C_CA%2C_USA_%2852075715442%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Totality during the lunar eclipse of 15 May 2022. Direct sunlight is being blocked by the Earth, and the only light reaching it is sunlight refracted by Earth's atmosphere, producing a reddish color.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFull_Eclipse_of_the_Moon_as_seen_in_from_Irvine%2C_CA%2C_USA_(52075715442)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Eclipse_from_moon.jpg/500px-Eclipse_from_moon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c